note The frame's two camera hooks, side by side. The fit runs here rather than inside the graph because it needs the font metrics: the layout is already done in cells, so it walks the font size down until the tree's cell box fits the canvas, sets the zoom to exactly that size over the UI size (so graph_px reproduces it), and pans to the tree's top-left. Everything else the camera does is move_camera, called once this frame's cell size is recorded, so rect_px can give it pixel rectangles.

