note The anchor a node button sets before its tree changes shape: the node and its pixel position that frame. After the relayout the pan moves by the node's displacement, so expanding or hiding its callees or callers, or collapsing it, leaves it and the button under the pointer exactly where they were; the new nodes appear beside it and the reader pans if they run off the canvas.

